rly 20th century, many physicists perceived a crisis: anomalies such as blackbody radiation, the Michelson–Morley null result, and observations of discrete atomic spectra conflicted with classical predictions, and new frameworks—such as Einstein’s special relativity and the emerging quantum theory—were beginning to replace them…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://thelivingfossils.substack.com/p/psychologys-greatest-misses-part?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://thelivingfossils.substack.com/p/psychologys-greatest-misses-part?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-913">Political Psychology Links, 1/12/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://thelivingfossils.substack.com/p/psychologys-greatest-misses-part?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://thelivingfossils.substack.com/p/psychologys-greatest-misses-part?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Jan 2026 13:03:42 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Software Too Cheap to Meter]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>In a 1954 speech, the chairman of the US Atomic Energy Commission famously predicted that “our children will enjoy in their homes electrical energy too cheap to meter”. He was wrong, of course; the era of unlimited electricity didn’t arrive. But we are approaching the era of unmetered software…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://secondthoughts.ai/p/software-too-cheap-to-meter?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://secondthoughts.ai/p/software-too-cheap-to-meter?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1112026">AI Links, 1/11/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://secondthoughts.ai/p/software-too-cheap-to-meter?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://secondthoughts.ai/p/software-too-cheap-to-meter?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Jan 2026 13:03:07 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Claude Code and What Comes Next]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>I opened Claude Code and gave it the command: “Develop a web-based or software-based startup idea that will make me $1000 a month where you do all the work by generating the idea and implementing it. i shouldn’t have to do anything at all except run some program you give me once. it shouldn’t require any coding knowledge on my part, so make sure everyth…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/claude-code-and-what-comes-next?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/claude-code-and-what-comes-next?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1112026">AI Links, 1/11/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/claude-code-and-what-comes-next?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/claude-code-and-what-comes-next?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Jan 2026 13:03:07 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[I can't stop yelling at Claude Code]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>They say that if you really want to know a person’s character, you should observe how she treats her servants. On Christmas vacation, I realized I didn’t like what this said about me…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/i-cant-stop-yelling-at-claude-code?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/i-cant-stop-yelling-at-claude-code?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=w